## Setup & Installation

### 1. Enable External Apps in Termux
Inside Termux, allow Termux studio to send `RUN_COMMAND` intents:

```bash
mkdir -p ~/.termux
echo "allow-external-apps = true" >> ~/.termux/termux.properties
termux-reload-settings
termux-setup-storage
```

### 2. Install the `termux-studio` Package (`v1.0.0`)

#### Option A: Install directly from your local repo / shared folder
```bash
pkg install -y ./termux-repo/pool/main/t/termux-studio/termux-studio_1.0.0_all.deb
termux-studio link-storage
termux-studio probe
```

#### Option B: Install via `pkg` using GitHub Pages APT Repo
Enable GitHub Pages on your `termux-studio` repository (or host `termux-repo/`), then run in Termux:

```bash
echo "deb [trusted=yes] https://<YOUR_USERNAME>.github.io/termux-studio/termux-repo stable main" > $PREFIX/etc/apt/sources.list.d/termux-studio.list
pkg update -y
pkg install -y termux-studio
termux-studio link-storage
termux-studio probe
```

