## Building the Android APK

### Option A: Automated Build on GitHub Actions (No PC Required)
This repository includes `.github/workflows/build-apk.yml`.
1. Push this repository to GitHub.
2. Open the **Actions** tab on GitHub and wait for **Build Debug APK** to finish (or trigger it manually).
3. Download the **`termux-studio-v1.0.0-debug-apk`** artifact and install `app-debug.apk` on your Android phone.
4. Pushing a version tag (e.g., `git tag v1.0.0 && git push origin v1.0.0`) automatically attaches `app-debug.apk` to a GitHub Release.

### Option B: Local Build with Gradle
```bash
# Decode the included debug signing keystore (ignored by git)
base64 -d debug.keystore.base64 > debug.keystore

# Build debug APK
gradle assembleDebug
```
The compiled APK will be generated at:
`app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk`

